Run the scripts from the top of the source tree; the images are created in ..

Create singularity images (once, or to update Debian unstable) :
- singularity-create-build.sh : build image ../singularity.glgrib-build (compilers, CMake, debhelper,
  build dependencies)
- singularity-create-install.sh : install/test image ../singularity.glgrib-install

Build :
- singularity-build.sh (enter build container)
- debian-build.sh (run from build container); build the Debian packages with CMake
  (dh --buildsystem=cmake) from the upstream tarball made by scripts/debian/tar.pl (files tracked by
  git only), in ../debian-build; the packages are moved to ..
  Without entering the container :
    singularity exec --bind $HOME/tmp:/tmp ../singularity.glgrib-build ./scripts/singularity/debian-build.sh

Install :
- singularity-install.sh (enter install/test container)
- debian-install.sh (run from install/test container); install glgrib-glfw from the packages in ..
  Debian unstable ships glgrib too: the version in packaging/debian/changelog must be higher than the
  archive's, or apt installs the archive packages.

Test :
- singularity-test.sh (enter test container)
- debian-test.sh (run from test container); start glgrib-glfw

Developer build in the build container, without packaging :
  singularity exec ../singularity.glgrib-build sh -c 'cmake -S . -B build/debian && cmake --build build/debian -j'
